==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|lang=grc|δέον||that which is binding, needful, right, proper}} + [[λόγος]] (argument).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{ethics}} The [[ethical]] study of [[duties]], [[obligation]]s, and [[right]]s, with an approach focusing on the [[rightness]] or [[wrongness]] of actions themselves and not on the [[goodness]] or [[badness]] of the [[consequence]]s of those actions.

